  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the celebratory scene of Black children",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual and textual scene of two Black children joyfully playing in water, with the text 'celebrating the weekend like' implying that the user's own weekend celebration is being compared to or equated with the children's spontaneous, uninhibited joy. This projection is implicit, as the meme invites the viewer to imagine themselves in the children's position or to see their own weekend celebration through the lens of the children's 'basic' or 'primitive' play. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the meme creates a direct identification or comparison, projecting the user's experience onto the scene.",
